  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "deep dubstep (the early south London sound): half-time snare on three, a kick that skips around it, shuffled sixteenth hats with heavy swing, and a sub that holds low and long",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars: the snare on three, the kick on one and skipping to the a of two in the second bar; closed sixteenths swung hard and a quieter shaker under them, the shuffle this sound is known for. The sub holds two long notes a phrase. At 130 under the Dub key."
  }
